#: 128b133effce46108acfa01da1586d80
msgid "COMPASS\\_ORIENT: Compass orientation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:23164
#: b015952941ef4ff7be9a1848bbcc747b
msgid "The orientation of the first external compass relative to the vehicle frame\\. This value will be ignored unless this compass is set as an external compass\\. When set correctly in the northern hemisphere\\, pointing the nose and right side down should increase the MagX and MagY values respectively\\. Rolling the vehicle upside down should decrease the MagZ value\\. For southern hemisphere\\, switch increase and decrease\\. NOTE\\: For internal compasses\\, AHRS\\_ORIENT is used\\. The label for each option is specified in the order of rotations for that orientation\\. Firmware versions 4\\.2 and prior can use a CUSTOM \\(100\\) rotation to set the COMPASS\\_CUS\\_ROLL\\/PIT\\/YAW angles for Compass orientation\\. Later versions provide two general custom rotations which can be used\\, Custom 1 and Custom 2\\, with CUST\\_1\\_ROLL\\/PIT\\/YAW or CUST\\_2\\_ROLL\\/PIT\\/YAW angles\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:23274
#: 39b7553887084a868f1838c63eab9a86
msgid "COMPASS\\_EXTERNAL: Compass is attached via an external cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:23278
#: 1dfd5c3da3e34dd8aa23fdf8d275fc6b
msgid "Configure compass so it is attached externally\\. This is auto\\-detected on most boards\\. Set to 1 if the compass is externally connected\\. When externally connected the COMPASS\\_ORIENT option operates independently of the AHRS\\_ORIENTATION board orientation option\\. If set to 0 or 1 then auto\\-detection by bus connection can override the value\\. If set to 2 then auto\\-detection will be disabled\\."
msgstr ""

