#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:23617
#: cc09296c65c54ace810e95b02fcb8953
msgid "The orientation of a second external compass relative to the vehicle frame\\. This value will be ignored unless this compass is set as an external compass\\. When set correctly in the northern hemisphere\\, pointing the nose and right side down should increase the MagX and MagY values respectively\\. Rolling the vehicle upside down should decrease the MagZ value\\. For southern hemisphere\\, switch increase and decrease\\. NOTE\\: For internal compasses\\, AHRS\\_ORIENT is used\\. The label for each option is specified in the order of rotations for that orientation\\. Firmware versions 4\\.2 and prior can use a CUSTOM \\(100\\) rotation to set the COMPASS\\_CUS\\_ROLL\\/PIT\\/YAW angles for Compass orientation\\. Later versions provide two general custom rotations which can be used\\, Custom 1 and Custom 2\\, with CUST\\_1\\_ROLL\\/PIT\\/YAW or CUST\\_2\\_ROLL\\/PIT\\/YAW angles\\."
msgstr ""

