#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31704
#: 7d48788705a246e88d7871e59cf0d12d
msgid "Bitmap of what Logger backend types to enable\\. Block\\-based logging is available on SITL and boards with dataflash chips\\. Multiple backends can be selected\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31713
#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:79152
#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:79550
#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:79948
#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:80346
#: 66d0ceecfc0649f09e1f4826423c23f2
#: f7b3feb255b249ac92e1ae2740f1bd39
#: 2fac6b3a8f1c4e58a4e8a4928a3569d5
#: 3c3e4ee6a20941bb9960f6208960d982
#: c693e9e41fbe43bcb3efcd01c8b5125f
msgid "File"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31717
#: aed43792a53f4b9f884a00b27f4291d5
msgid "Block"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31728
#: 8e7e470eed0e4411927d11d610c9871b
msgid "LOG\\_FILE\\_BUFSIZE: Logging File and Block Backend buffer size max \\(in kibibytes\\)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31731
#: b96b5de1dda9497890a0ef53892927eb
msgid "The File and Block backends use a buffer to store data before writing to the block device\\.  Raising this value may reduce \\\"gaps\\\" in your SD card logging but increases memory usage\\.  This buffer size may be reduced to free up available memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31737
#: c12f9e2805e54f29a2cacb3e5323583d
msgid "4 to 200"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31737
#: 5f555b4441e04e0693ecf35df0dae44c
msgid "kibibytes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31746
#: 3283b07f7c9146c8b198ea3543895418
msgid "LOG\\_DISARMED: Enable logging while disarmed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31749
#: f2a084441a514dcc971f6306f1cc2981
msgid "If LOG\\_DISARMED is set to 1 then logging will be enabled at all times including when disarmed\\. Logging before arming can make for very large logfiles but can help a lot when tracking down startup issues and is necessary if logging of EKF replay data is selected via the LOG\\_REPLAY parameter\\. If LOG\\_DISARMED is set to 2\\, then logging will be enabled when disarmed\\, but not if a USB connection is detected\\. This can be used to prevent unwanted data logs being generated when the vehicle is connected via USB for log downloading or parameter changes\\. If LOG\\_DISARMED is set to 3 then logging will happen while disarmed\\, but if the vehicle never arms then the logs using the filesystem backend will be discarded on the next boot\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31762
#: 088036fb830049af8e4e300a2646803a
msgid "Disabled on USB connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31764
#: bcb0b54b0b1945aeba1518c237807e04
msgid "Discard log on reboot if never armed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31775
#: 916e7218bf9e447284306ca742e50d41
msgid "LOG\\_REPLAY: Enable logging of information needed for Replay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31778
#: 1e1a1cae33f94706b2bf5b69433355fe
msgid "If LOG\\_REPLAY is set to 1 then the EKF2 and EKF3 state estimators will log detailed information needed for diagnosing problems with the Kalman filter\\. LOG\\_DISARMED must be set to 1 or 2 or else the log will not contain the pre\\-flight data required for replay testing of the EKF\\'s\\. It is suggested that you also raise LOG\\_FILE\\_BUFSIZE to give more buffer space for logging and use a high quality microSD card to ensure no sensor data is lost\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31800
#: c1357bde07fd45a581cceaf1369711ee
msgid "LOG\\_FILE\\_DSRMROT: Stop logging to current file on disarm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31803
#: 5dc19688e75c4bcbb57f4ed490abbe8e
msgid "When set\\, the current log file is closed when the vehicle is disarmed\\.  If LOG\\_DISARMED is set then a fresh log will be opened\\. Applies to the File and Block logging backends\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31825
#: 5d7b1590224b47e1be5c775d10252b3b
msgid "LOG\\_MAV\\_BUFSIZE: Maximum AP\\_Logger MAVLink Backend buffer size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31829
#: 3988248d30ce4f539ee77cebc06a7468
msgid "Maximum amount of memory to allocate to AP\\_Logger\\-over\\-mavlink"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31835
#: e8afeb938df541d5b09f176f06292d39
msgid "kilobytes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31844
#: 696b233fba15470a95e4cab5e111af93
msgid "LOG\\_FILE\\_TIMEOUT: Timeout before giving up on file writes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31847
#: 30f88656d5574b7bbfdfcef07cf62f6c
msgid "This controls the amount of time before failing writes to a log file cause the file to be closed and logging stopped\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31862
#: d13724bc7aa843eabcffb915042349b3
msgid "LOG\\_FILE\\_MB\\_FREE: Old logs on the SD card will be deleted to maintain this amount of free space"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31865
#: b61a9d6fbb3d4cff85ed7511ce2d7402
msgid "Set this such that the free space is larger than your largest typical flight log"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31871
#: 4c99df579f1742f4a712ed82d7dc5e63
msgid "2 to 1000"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31871
#: 326e2fc312f348b385e79024ca2a9c02
msgid "megabyte"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31880
#: d8667e074acc463ab68e4d0a39e302e1
msgid "LOG\\_FILE\\_RATEMAX: Maximum logging rate for file backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31883
#: 957cff6d36e5443583a21bf8827f7667
msgid "This sets the maximum rate that streaming log messages will be logged to the file backend\\. A value of zero means that rate limiting is disabled\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31898
#: 9b65ebf932a349b3a97c9aa9cea15449
msgid "LOG\\_MAV\\_RATEMAX: Maximum logging rate for mavlink backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31901
#: 61cf89f7757044e4b3194601ad73423d
msgid "This sets the maximum rate that streaming log messages will be logged to the mavlink backend\\. A value of zero means that rate limiting is disabled\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31916
#: 60961fe634c04e6f8ac36cdd11627d01
msgid "LOG\\_BLK\\_RATEMAX: Maximum logging rate for block backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31919
#: d89d398e1a3d419a9088d8de91ba62eb
msgid "This sets the maximum rate that streaming log messages will be logged to the block backend\\. A value of zero means that rate limiting is disabled\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31934
#: 7d2658cc71104a8ba5bb282801e91fc9
msgid "LOG\\_DARM\\_RATEMAX: Maximum logging rate when disarmed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31937
#: d1d777004d5a46e2bad90948ffdd0aeb
msgid "This sets the maximum rate that streaming log messages will be logged to any backend when disarmed\\. A value of zero means that the normal backend rate limit is applied\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31952
#: 447ae20153c84ad0b52a63e9505e6676
msgid "LOG\\_MAX\\_FILES: Maximum number of log files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31957
#: 4536d92bc06240458a5bd4b9df71f58a
msgid "This sets the maximum number of log file that will be written on dataflash or sd card before starting to rotate log number\\. Limit is capped at 500 logs\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31963
#: 1f381e28a8ba4a579d15a6dcf0ba43cd
msgid "2 to 500"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31973
#: d80a478d73d244cdaba01c0eeed970bf
msgid "MAV Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31979
#: 73b1ede43e054692a1854bbd9b391db7
msgid "MAV\\_SYSID: MAVLink system ID of this vehicle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31983
#: df91ea4bf4954f708badf9468c5d50c5
msgid "Allows setting an individual MAVLink system id for this vehicle to distinguish it from others on the same network\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31989
#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:32008
#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:84344
#: 4fcefc4944074cb09b759ba9cb33af23
#: 87e9338adbfd4af9b7e0725590e175ea
#: 37c9c42ccfdf4712b5b6323ff4f4a694
msgid "1 to 255"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:31998
#: 828e7d76593c4d26935d368343dedbbb
msgid "MAV\\_GCS\\_SYSID: My ground station number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:32002
#: d6bb98bc7ded453981bf36896c9bcf8a
msgid "This sets what MAVLink source system IDs are accepted for GCS failsafe handling\\, RC overrides and manual control\\. When MAV\\_GCS\\_SYSID\\_HI is less than MAV\\_GCS\\_SYSID then only this value is considered to be a GCS\\. When MAV\\_GCS\\_SYSID\\_HI is greater than or equal to MAV\\_GCS\\_SYSID then the range of values between MAV\\_GCS\\_SYSID and MAV\\_GCS\\_SYSID\\_HI \\(inclusive\\) are all treated as valid GCS MAVLink system IDs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:32017
#: a9c72f3c54894193819da10291d26d8a
msgid "MAV\\_GCS\\_SYSID\\_HI: ground station system ID\\, maximum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/AP_Periph-Parameters.rst:32021
#: 0f1827085e1c4aa3b8c6a5fcaf759680
msgid "Upper limit of MAVLink source system IDs considered to be from the GCS\\. When this is less than MAV\\_GCS\\_SYSID then only MAV\\_GCS\\_SYSID is used as GCS ID\\. When this is greater than or equal to MAV\\_GCS\\_SYSID then the range of values from MAV\\_GCS\\_SYSID to MAV\\_GCS\\_SYSID\\_HI \\(inclusive\\) is treated as a GCS ID\\."
msgstr ""

